  "releaseNotes": "Extended UpdateEnergyUsageAsync for SMART energy-monitoring v2 devices that implement only a subset of the advertised methods. It now prefers get_emeter_data, falls back to get_energy_usage, and requests get_current_power only when needed; unknown-method and invalid-parameters responses are handled as optional-method failures while genuine device errors still surface. Added the 2500-9000 K color-temperature feature range for newer-firmware KL400L5 light strips. Legacy and SMART v1 behavior is unchanged. No breaking API changes.",
